# HANGTEST=nandmb (docs/kernel/nandboot_hang_analysis.md, hang 12): nandtick
# (tick check, PC samples, NAND trace, ramoops, hang watchdog) with
# mv61x0.mc_drain=0: mb()/wmb(), and so every writel(), no longer writes
# the DDR controller's drain register (+0x530, the vendor's "cache sync").
# Switchable at run time: /sys/module/mv61x0/parameters/mc_drain.
# DEBUG IMAGE ONLY: it arms a hardware watchdog, so each run needs the
# owner's OK.
# - timer_mv61x0.hang_wdt=30: timer 0 resets the board 30 s after the last
#   kick (a kworker kicks every 5 s), so a hard hang reboots by itself;
# - pstore/ramoops in 1 MB at 0x1e000000: the console log of the boot
#   before;
# - marvell_nand.trace_phys=0x1e100000 (patch 0015): the last 126 NAND
#   controller steps in a 4 KB no-map area, printed by the next boot of
#   this image (nandboot-nanddbg.dts reserves both areas).
# Both only help if this same image boots after the reset (mtd0, or a RAM
# boot from U-Boot before the stock autoboot).
CONFIG_CMDLINE="console=ttyS0,115200n8 marvell_nand.write_window=1741,4091 panic=10 consoleblank=0 timer_mv61x0.hang_wdt=30 marvell_nand.trace_phys=0x1e100000 timer_mv61x0.tick_check=100 mv61x0.mc_drain=0"
CONFIG_PSTORE=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_PMSG=y
